{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790009514,"nonce":"6nxNcFKXkZfrigdMlO9X9BhcTFc=","title":"Story: Shared saved views, and rules that fire without a daemon","message":"Outcome: named views — query, sort, grouping — that everyone on the team shares instead of retyping, and automation rules that act on the op log when something happens, all without the daemon AGENTS.md rules out.\n\nBoth live in the same config entity as the schema and the flow catalogue (7c90fbd): views and rules are aliases too, and per-key ops mean two people adding two different views both survive.\n\nThe tension this story has to resolve is real. 'No daemon' and 'when X happens, do Y' pull against each other, so a rule can only be evaluated somewhere a process already exists: opportunistically at the end of any mutating command, inside a long-lived webui/TUI through the ref watcher (63c68d1), or on a schedule in CI. Each fires late, and two of them can fire twice, so actions must be idempotent and each rule needs a watermark over the op log rather than a 'did it happen' flag.\n\nNote 8573d99 (flow pr: transition on open/merge) is a hardcoded instance of exactly one rule. The engine should subsume it rather than sit beside it.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790009514,"nonce":"/yymjd363CZpBwfdpHbrX6xYtv0=","key":"type","value":"story"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790009514,"nonce":"v4gHsGohDLtyV3ytKZlMTV0quJM=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}